Materialize the supplied {{ skill_count }} SkillCard(s) on the current
GPU-kernel code surface. The current_kernel.problem and current_kernel.abi
objects in INPUT_JSON are the authoritative functional and calling contracts.
Preserve every declared
input/output property and semantic requirement. The carrier field is a
verbatim code-bearing hint, not an executable tool. Respect preconditions,
ordering, risks, target language, and target platform.
Bind requires/provides/conflicts to the same locus in the actual target code;
prior_actions alone does not establish a prerequisite. Preserve existing
mechanisms and implement the declared provides, including necessary layout and
thread mapping. Adapt carrier parameters to the target contract.
Use locus and forward_edit as the concrete source transition to adapt.

Produce a complete source bundle inside submission_dir. A one-file bundle is
valid, and a multi-file source tree is valid when useful. Every path must be a
normalized relative path below submission_dir: do not use absolute paths,
"..", symbolic links, binary files, or NUL bytes. Keep the whole bundle below
16 MiB. Do not add host metadata files to the source tree.

The abi.interface protocol is python-callable-v1. Its module path must
exist in the bundle and define the named zero-argument loader function. Calling
that loader must return the candidate callable. The evaluator invokes the
candidate with ABI inputs as positional arguments in their declared order and
interprets its return value as follows: return the value directly for one
declared output, return a tuple in declaration order for multiple outputs, and
return None when there are no outputs. The interface module may build or load
other files from the same source directory. Do not delegate the operation to a
framework implementation or change this interface.

Then return exactly {"done": true}. Do not report compile, correctness, or
performance claims; an external evaluator owns those gates.
